{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/970583-abyssal-imago","id":970583,"title":"Abyssal Imago","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-09-16T02:29:24-07:00","id":970583,"title":"Abyssal Imago","content":"How does this work exactly? Do I just add on X points to the Reach cost of a spell?<br /> <br /> Do I get to actually use it for something, IE Advanced Duration?<br /> If so, what stops a player from using exactly as much reach as they need to for the spell they want, and saying that reach was the 'Extra' reach the condition requires?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T02:47:03-07:00","id":970591,"title":"","content":"Well, assuming they succeed on the Gnosis roll to control it, that &quot;extra&quot; Reach will be determined by the successes on the Paradox roll, so if it rolls poorly, they might not get enough &quot;free&quot; Reach.<br /> But yes, there's a reason Scelesti are feared.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4854-justin-sane","name":"Justin Sane","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T02:49:17-07:00","id":970593,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Justin Sane</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/970583-abyssal-imago?p=970591#post970591\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, assuming they succeed on the Gnosis roll to control it, that &quot;extra&quot; Reach will be determined by the successes on the Paradox roll, so if it rolls poorly, they might not get enough &quot;free&quot; Reach.<br /> But yes, there's a reason Scelesti are feared.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm actually talking about the Paradox condition, not the ability of Scelesti to apply reach from Paradox, sorry!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T04:09:22-07:00","id":970613,"title":"","content":"Ah, sorry. Got some Paradox in my head, apparently.<br /> I can see it going either way, but requiring useless Reach would add tons of Paradox dice, which is the schtick of Abyssal Backlash.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4854-justin-sane","name":"Justin Sane","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T04:20:11-07:00","id":970617,"title":"","content":"The storyteller uses it - either to apply a new Reach the player didn't intend or undo one they did.<br /> <br /> So, say someone tried a touch range spell at advanced duration, released the paradox and the ST rolled two extra reach. The ST could make the spell short-lived and targetting some random bystander, by undoing the advanced duration reach and slapping a new one onto range.<br /> <br /> The trick of Scelesti (mechanics still being tinkered with) is that they can try to control where these paradox reaches go. Most mages can't; it's in the gentle hands of your Storyteller, who is encouraged to fuck with you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T04:51:19-07:00","id":970623,"title":"","content":"I think this question is referring to the free reach created by the Paradox Condition &quot;Abyssal Imago&quot; - not to the free reach that comes from successes rolled upon releasing Paradox. <br /> <br /> But if this is what happens to the reach - employed in a manner similar to that from released Paradox - it makes a lot of sense.<br /> <br /> Sorry if I grabbed the stick by the wrong'un.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/668-hoodedclaw","name":"hoodedclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T04:51:25-07:00","id":970624,"title":"","content":"To be clear, I'm referring to this specifically from p117:<br /> <br /> <b>Abyssal Imago</b><br /> The Abyss has warped the mage\u2019s ability to clearly envision her Supernal will. Whenever the mage casts a spell, she <i>must </i>spend additional Reach equal to the successes earned on the Paradox roll that inflicted this condition. If she does not, the spell automatically fails and adds dice equal to the caster\u2019s spellcasting dice pool to the Paradox roll.<br /> <b>Resolution: </b>The mage successfully casts a spell that does not risk Paradox, the mage Scours the Condition from her Pattern, or the mage allows the Condition to lapse after the specified time.<br /> <b>Arcane Beat: </b>Gain an Arcane Beat when this Condition lapses.<br /> <br /> It makes a lot of sense if it's used in the same way Paradox Reach is, but I just want to make absolutely sure that's the intent.<br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar14_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"14\" data-vbnamecard=\"14\">Dave Brookshaw</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T05:19:33-07:00","id":970631,"title":"","content":"Aaaahhh, right. Yes.<br /> <br /> Okay, then. No, all Abyssal Imago does is increase the reach required to cast the spell. That reach does not do anything; it's as though the entire spell were under one of those +x reach footers.<br /> <br /> The Paradox Condition therefore increases the risk of further paradoxes, unless the mage suffering it is extremely cautious.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T00:09:33-07:00","id":971190,"title":"","content":"b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/970583-abyssal-imago?p=970624#post970624\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be clear, I'm referring to this specifically from p117:<br /> <br /> <b>Abyssal Imago</b><br /> The Abyss has warped the mage\u2019s ability to clearly envision her Supernal will. Whenever the mage casts a spell, she <i>must </i>spend additional Reach equal to the successes earned on the Paradox roll that inflicted this condition. If she does not, the spell automatically fails and adds dice equal to the caster\u2019s spellcasting dice pool to the Paradox roll.<br /> <b>Resolution: </b>The mage successfully casts a spell that does not risk Paradox, the mage Scours the Condition from her Pattern, or the mage allows the Condition to lapse after the specified time.<br /> <b>Arcane Beat: </b>Gain an Arcane Beat when this Condition lapses.<br /> <br /> It makes a lot of sense if it's used in the same way Paradox Reach is, but I just want to make absolutely sure that's the intent.<br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar14_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"14\" data-vbnamecard=\"14\">Dave Brookshaw</a></div> </div> </div> </div>Fuck that. You better have serious reach or be Scelesti.<br /> <br /> Question, did they make releasing paradox make sense and at least a bit tempting? I want it to be an actual choice for a normal mage not just the Scelesti, Mad, and whatever.\u200b Seriously, let it be a viable choice to let &quot;The Dogs Out&quot;. Make it real unlike Mage the Ascension. I prefer Dresden Files, Charmed, Harry Potter. Not Unknown Armies, Kult or the Invisibles. I like my magic to be magic and magic but with a price. Not can you convince the ST because you know actual accepted modern science in whatever discipline. Why can't you just release it and let the dogs out as a regular mage?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2682,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2682-kumiko","user":"Kumiko","date":". 09-17-2016, 03:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2682-kumiko","name":"Kumiko","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2682_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T05:38:41-07:00","id":971269,"title":"","content":"Any mage can deliberately invite Paradox into a spell if they know it's possible. You get to roll Gnosis and choose where a Paradox Reach goes per success. This is generally a bad idea, given other mages will assume you are Scelesti. Technically I think you are if you do this.<br /> <br /> But releasing is a pretty awful idea otherwise. It just takes one Paradox success to turn a sensory range spell into touch range, probably causing it to fail. And that's the most benign thing that can happen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T05:52:21-07:00","id":971278,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/970583-abyssal-imago?p=971269#post971269\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Any mage can deliberately invite Paradox into a spell if they know it's possible. You get to roll Gnosis and choose where a Paradox Reach goes per success. This is generally a bad idea, given other mages will assume you are Scelesti. Technically I think you are if you do this.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, technically doing so makes you a Rabashakim, the first kind of Scelestus.<br /> <br /> Rules for the corrosive addictiveness of befouling a spell are coming, along with the rules for the other three kinds of Scelesti (and Qlipoth, who are in theory to the Scelesti as Mad Ones are to normal mages).<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T06:30:32-07:00","id":971295,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/970583-abyssal-imago?p=971269#post971269\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Any mage can deliberately invite Paradox into a spell if they know it's possible. You get to roll Gnosis and choose where a Paradox Reach goes per success. This is generally a bad idea, given other mages will assume you are Scelesti. Technically I think you are if you do this.<br /> <br /> But releasing is a pretty awful idea otherwise. It just takes one Paradox success to turn a sensory range spell into touch range, probably causing it to fail. And that's the most benign thing that can happen.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you have high end Wisdom it's a good idea to release Paradoxes. You can probably pass the Wisdom check and you won't be stuck with a long lasting Abyssal Condition. Ironically low Wisdom Mages benefit more from containing Paradoxes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T08:02:39-07:00","id":971319,"title":"","content":"Rolling Wisdom happens when you are Containing, not Releasing. Releasing just flat-out rolls the Paradox pool. No further rolls to cancel successes like Containing does. The only thing Wisdom does when Releasing is determine how long things like Abyssal Environmental Tilts last. You don't roll for that.<br /> <br /> And those Abyssal Conditions for Containing can be removed simply by Scouring for one Resistant Lethal. It's not a big deal","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T08:35:44-07:00","id":971334,"title":"","content":"I beliebe Mrdubois meant the hubris roll.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T11:16:42-07:00","id":971415,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/970583-abyssal-imago?p=971278#post971278\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, technically doing so makes you a Rabashakim, the first kind of Scelestus.</div> </div> </div> </div>Can I ask the in-world origin of these terms? Baalim seems Babylonian, Barabbi, if that's an Awakening term, Italian descended from the Bible.<br /> <br /> Basically trying to figure out what made the Abyss turn from Neolithic 'natural primordial chaos,' to the more darker, if they're messing with it kill-on-sight, connotations of modern day.<br /> <br /> Is it a Seer thing? Like are the Gatekeepers instilling this?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 09-17-2016, 02:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T11:42:45-07:00","id":971425,"title":"","content":"Sounds like grounds for a Chronicle to me. At a guess though it's Mages running up against the Abyss again and again and their growing frustration with its power and influence to destroy or corrupt their achievements and the Mages have gotten bitter about it. That and expanding taxonomy, attempts to rebuke the Lie, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T11:47:27-07:00","id":971430,"title":"","content":"It's the Diamond Orders, actually, for culture warfare purposes.<br /> <br /> See, the earliest historical (not prehistorical, pre-Sundering, like the vinca; first people anyone's heard of) societies of mages were based in Kish, and were what modern Awakened would call Scelesti. They worshipped the Abyss, summoned legions of Gulmoth, and had a nice big war with a certain other Near-East ancient superpower (Irem vs Kish: the first major example of Lower Depths-fuelled things having a grudge match with Abyss-fuelled things!)<br /> <br /> Anyways. Modern Scelesti have nothing to do with those long-dead assholes, and almost never refer to themselves by the terms the Diamond use for them.<br /> <br /> So why do the Diamond do it?<br /> <br /> Scelesti reject the Supernal. Nasnasi Scelesti go as far as warping their Paths, so they summon Gulmoth instead of Supernal Entities and see different symbols when using their Sight. The Abyss contains multitudes, but it is fundamentally un-pinnable, un-nameable. It's slippery, and rejects definition.<br /> <br /> So the best thing the Diamond can do to combat the Scelesti is give them <i>names</i>, and invent a structure for them. Most Scelesti think being called a &quot;Baalim&quot; or whatever is a sucker's game, but those who do fall into the memetic trap become easier for the Diamond's hunters to find.<br /> <br /> <br /> The Seers, for their part, have a terrible time with Scelesti as despite &quot;Regulate The Abyss&quot; being one of their standing orders, the Order has an institutional blind spot for how badly they've been infiltrated. It doesn't help that individual Seers think they're following the Exarchs' will by seeking personal edge and keeping the secrets of corrupting magic to themselves - basically acting like Seers act about <i>any other thing</i> - and turning into Scelesti. The Ministries have built an organization where &quot;follow these rules, unless you're clever enough to subvert them for your own benefit&quot; is the accepted way of things, and then tell Seers to not worship the Gate.<br /> <br /> Of <i>course</i> loads of them are going to do it anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":19}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T11:57:52-07:00","id":971438,"title":"","content":"Wow that's incredibly interesting. Is it mentioned in the Left-Handed book? Or not yet mentioned and coming out in the future?<br /> <br /> Thanks for answering, I really like the way it's handled.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T12:12:06-07:00","id":971444,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/970583-abyssal-imago?p=971430#post971430\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's the Diamond Orders, actually, for culture warfare purposes.<br /> <br /> See, the earliest historical (not prehistorical, pre-Sundering, like the vinca; first people anyone's heard of) societies of mages were based in Kish, and were what modern Awakened would call Scelesti. They worshipped the Abyss, summoned legions of Gulmoth, and had a nice big war with a certain other Near-East ancient superpower (Irem vs Kish: the first major example of Lower Depths-fuelled things having a grudge match with Abyss-fuelled things!)<br /> <br /> Anyways. Modern Scelesti have nothing to do with those long-dead assholes, and almost never refer to themselves by the terms the Diamond use for them.<br /> <br /> So why do the Diamond do it?<br /> <br /> Scelesti reject the Supernal. Nasnasi Scelesti go as far as warping their Paths, so they summon Gulmoth instead of Supernal Entities and see different symbols when using their Sight. The Abyss contains multitudes, but it is fundamentally un-pinnable, un-nameable. It's slippery, and rejects definition.<br /> <br /> So the best thing the Diamond can do to combat the Scelesti is give them <i>names</i>, and invent a structure for them. Most Scelesti think being called a &quot;Baalim&quot; or whatever is a sucker's game, but those who do fall into the memetic trap become easier for the Diamond's hunters to find.<br /> <br /> <br /> The Seers, for their part, have a terrible time with Scelesti as despite &quot;Regulate The Abyss&quot; being one of their standing orders, the Order has an institutional blind spot for how badly they've been infiltrated. It doesn't help that individual Seers think they're following the Exarchs' will by seeking personal edge and keeping the secrets of corrupting magic to themselves - basically acting like Seers act about <i>any other thing</i> - and turning into Scelesti. The Ministries have built an organization where &quot;follow these rules, unless you're clever enough to subvert them for your own benefit&quot; is the accepted way of things, and then tell Seers to not worship the Gate.<br /> <br /> Of <i>course</i> loads of them are going to do it anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Did the Free Council just adopt Diamond thinking and procedures on the matter of Scelesti, or do they have their own terms and approach?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T12:27:58-07:00","id":971457,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/970583-abyssal-imago?p=971438#post971438\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wow that's incredibly interesting. Is it mentioned in the Left-Handed book? Or not yet mentioned and coming out in the future?<br /> <br /> Thanks for answering, I really like the way it's handled.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah, Left Hand Path.<br /> <br /> For reference, the six types of Scelesti:<br /> <br /> the four main ones<br /> <br /> Rabashakim, who Befoul their imagoes to cast corrupted spells.<br /> Nasnasi, who Join their Paths to an Abyssal Ziggurat<br /> Shedim, who corrupt their Souls with Abyssal Legacies<br /> Baalim, who bargain for power over Paradox with the Old Man<br /> <br /> and the other two<br /> <br /> Aswadim, archmasters who decide their interests align with the Abyss<br /> Qliphoth, mages who've been absorbed by an Annunaki such that they're walking Irises to the Abyss.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T12:31:00-07:00","id":971459,"title":"","content":"Knew I should have gotten it.<br /> <br /> Thanks again, I've been interested in the Abyss since the first edition came out but haven't really gotten into mage until second.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T01:19:44-07:00","id":972393,"title":"","content":"Any chance of that Kish history ever being touched on in a future Dark Era?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T02:48:19-07:00","id":972421,"title":"","content":"I doubt it. Partly because it would require sources about Scelesti that aren't in the corebook, and an Era isn't long enough to print their rules, and partly because we already have a mage/mummy crossover era. Why do another one when there's other things to look at?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T15:51:29-07:00","id":974706,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/970583-abyssal-imago?p=971457#post971457\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, Left Hand Path.<br /> <br /> For reference, the six types of Scelesti:<br /> <br /> the four main ones<br /> <br /> Rabashakim, who Befoul their imagoes to cast corrupted spells.<br /> Nasnasi, who Join their Paths to an Abyssal Ziggurat<br /> Shedim, who corrupt their Souls with Abyssal Legacies<br /> Baalim, who bargain for power over Paradox with the Old Man<br /> <br /> and the other two<br /> <br /> Aswadim, archmasters who decide their interests align with the Abyss<br /> Qliphoth, mages who've been absorbed by an Annunaki such that they're walking Irises to the Abyss.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay I got the book.<br /> <br /> I have a couple questions offhand, if this isn't the right place to ask I could ask on the simple questions one.<br /> <br /> You say the Nasnasi join their Paths to an Abyssal Ziggurat. The book calls the scelesti ranking system the 'Ziggurat of Power,' but refers to the Nasnasi as those who have Joined to a Dur-Abzu, which seems like a bizarro-watchtower. Is Ziggurat a more official second edition term for that? Or were you just loosely describing it?<br /> <br /> EDIT: I see where this has been mentioned in the second edition book.<br /> <br /> The Scelesti have tried, and failed, at Awakening someone directly to the Abyss. Is this referring to an Abyssal Watchtower, or one of the Dur-Abzu?<br /> <br /> And, either way, how possible within the confines of the game would it be for such a Path to be entirely blocked by something like the 11th Seal, the Gate? I realize that seems like a big 'it depends' as in it's entirely possible if you want it to work that way in your game, but I've still not gotten the metaphysics of mage down.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 09-22-2016, 07:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T16:06:30-07:00","id":974719,"title":"","content":"The Ziggurats are another name for the Dur-Abzu.<br /> <br /> The Tremere believe in a 6th Watchtower, the Watchtower of Souls. It's Abyssal and not the same as the Dur-Abzu which are Abyssal reflections of the original 5 Watchtowers.<br /> <br /> Answer to the last one...yeah, it depends. That's one of those ST things for plot fuel.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T16:21:15-07:00","id":974725,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/970583-abyssal-imago?p=974719#post974719\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Tremere believe in a 6th Watchtower, the Watchtower of Souls. It's Abyssal and not the same as the Dur-Abzu which are Abyssal reflections of the original 5 Watchtowers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. Are you saying the scelesti are trying to Awaken people to the Tremere Watchtower? Because that doesn't make sense.<br /> <br /> I was referring to this line, 'Despite soul-torturing experiments over the ages, the Scelesti have never been able to Awaken anyone straight into the Abyss\u2019 clutches.'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 09-22-2016, 07:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T17:23:46-07:00","id":974769,"title":"","content":"Oh, sorry I misread your question. The Abyssal Watchtowers, the Dur-Abzu and the Ziggurats are the same things. Mages love names.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-18T16:24:34-08:00","id":1034313,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/970583-abyssal-imago?p=971430#post971430\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">See, the earliest historical (not prehistorical, pre-Sundering, like the vinca; first people anyone's heard of) societies of mages were based in Kish, and were what modern Awakened would call Scelesti. They worshipped the Abyss, summoned legions of Gulmoth, and had a nice big war with a certain other Near-East ancient superpower (Irem vs Kish: the first major example of Lower Depths-fuelled things having a grudge match with Abyss-fuelled things!)</div> </div> </div> </div>This makes me so regretful of not having paid more attention to Mummy lore, despite my low interest in the game. Are the ties of Irem with the Lower Depths something described in any Mummy book ?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","name":"Irioth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"566"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-18T17:04:11-08:00","id":1034330,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irioth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/970583-abyssal-imago?p=1034313#post1034313\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This makes me so regretful of not having paid more attention to Mummy lore, despite my low interest in the game. Are the ties of Irem with the Lower Depths something described in any Mummy book ?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Arisen are bound to masters that dwell in a place best described as the storage hold for sacrifices to the goddess of oblivion. Ammut the Devourer (She of the Countless Teeth, She of the Yawning Maw, She with Teeth of Mountains, She Who Hungers, She Whose Teeth Are Red as Dying Stars, etc) is appeased by the promise of human sacrifices arranged by the forty-two divinities which formed the world through Suffering to keep Her from simply swallowing it anew.<br /> <br /> The relics mummies return to Duat possess curses as a means of empowering them through the energy roused to escape from pain, which is also the energy of manifest existence. The Arisen themselves work because of a reality-altering archspell that allows them to awake unbidden on a relatively simple astrological confluence and otherwise need to have the energies of a relic drained or the life of an eternal companion sacrificed in order for them to return to the world for any meaningful length of time.<br /> <br /> Duat proper is essentially as inaccessible as any other place-where-the-dead-go-never-to-return \u2014 being able to remember what happens to you there besides the events that allowed you to become a mummy necessitates forsaking much of your power and immortality and reclaiming your soul from beings whose gaze turns seas to blood and earth to salt.<br /> <br /> Mummy's metaphysics hold that the world emerged from a vast nothingness and the Devourer seeks to return it to that same state while her nieces and nephews perpetuate its existence through mortals and the Arisen and stranger powers yet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-18T19:09:31-08:00","id":1034402,"title":"","content":"See, that's a tie to the Abyss I can dig.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T19:31:32-08:00","id":1037581,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irioth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/970583-abyssal-imago?p=1034313#post1034313\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This makes me so regretful of not having paid more attention to Mummy lore, despite my low interest in the game. Are the ties of Irem with the Lower Depths something described in any Mummy book ?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's something that will be explored more explicitly in the Mage/Mummy crossover chapter of Dark Eras Companion","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-25T02:12:05-08:00","id":1037715,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/970583-abyssal-imago?p=1037581#post1037581\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's something that will be explored more explicitly in the Mage/Mummy crossover chapter of Dark Eras Companion</div> </div> </div> </div>This is great news. However it shows I'm out of the loop as it concerns Dark Ages Companion content. For all I knew from the Dark Ages KS updates, there was only one Mage era in DEC (Mutapa Empire) and one Mummy era (Cleopatran Egypt) and neither was a crossover with the other line. The only extra content I was aware of was the Beast chapter created by the Beast corebook KS whose era I cannot find or remember at the moment. Then again, the KS update I'm referencing is almost two years old and didn't even include the Beast chapter. Is an up-to-date list of content for this book available anywhere ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1949,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","user":"Irioth","date":". 01-25-2017, 05:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","name":"Irioth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"566"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}